# by scripts/setup, not stored in git.
models/
*.onnx

# ─── Python bytecode (Kaggle kernels) ───
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ─── ARC-2026 generated artefacts ───────────────────────────
# kaggle-jobs/arc-2026-solver.generated.py is BUILT by scripts/arc-2026-push.sh from
# arc-2026/arc/*.py. Committing it would let the notebook drift from the solver the
# paper's numbers came from, which is the one failure mode this generator exists to
# prevent.
kaggle-jobs/arc-2026-solver.generated.py
# Third-party ARC task data (fetch-data.sh clones it) and per-run outputs.
arc-2026/data/
arc-2026/results/kaggle-*/
arc-2026/results/predictions*.json

# APK build (scripts/build-apk.sh) — self-signed release keys + _work temp; only the final APK in public/downloads is committed
# apk/build-<slug>/ is the store builder's temp working dir; apk/launcher/ is generated by gen-launcher-icons.js
apk/build/
apk/build-*/
apk/launcher/
apk/*.jks
apk/keystore.env
# Gradle Android Studio project — build artefacts and machine-local SDK path
apk/app/build/
apk/local.properties
apk/.gradle/
public/downloads/*.idsig
# AAB only for Play upload (not publicly hosted) — can be rebuilt
public/downloads/*.aab
# App APKs produced by Tukuk Builder (tukuk-km* = user-generated app slugs)
# — local artifacts on the server, can be rebuilt with
# scripts/build-apk.sh <slug>. Do not commit: files that exist untracked on the server
# will REJECT `git merge --ff-only` of tukuk-update.service.
public/downloads/tukuk-km*.apk
# Google Cloud service-account key for fastlane supply — SECRET, do not commit
google-cloud-key.json
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
# Tukuk Agent = code-server fork with its own history (nested repo, upstream detached)
code-server/
# Tukuk Builder = bolt.diy fork with its own history (nested repo, remote fevian448)
bolt.diy/
# ─── ONE FOLDER: the payloads that live INSIDE this checkout on the box ─────────────
# deploy/paths.sh makes the app folder the only folder on the server, so the Builder's
# clone, the published game, the Godot binary and the game source are SUBDIRECTORIES of
# this repo on the box (models/ is already ignored above). They are box-local data, not
# source: ignored here so `git status` stays quiet, and — more importantly — excluded
# from setup-all.sh's `rsync --delete` so "copy this checkout over that one" cannot
# delete 1-2 GB of Builder node_modules or the published game.
#
# /bin is NOT ignored wholesale, and test/repo-ignore-hygiene.test.js is why that was
# noticed: bin/tukuk-os.js is a TRACKED source file, so a bare `bin/` rule hid a real
# file from git (the test's "no tracked file is newly ignored" case). Only the Godot
# binary is payload. Same anchoring reason as /build/ below: an unanchored `bin/` would
# also match every node_modules bin directory.
/apps/
/bin/godot*
/game/
# Map-AI (git@github remote) and station-break (godot tps-demo fork) — same shape: each
# is a clone with its own origin, so the parent repo must never absorb them as a gitlink
Map-Ai---Version-1/
tps-demo/
# Local Godot build target for station-break (linux .so + binary) — rebuilt, never
# shipped. Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: unanchored `build/` also matches
# public/build/, and git then reports those TRACKED icons as ignored (verified with
# `git ls-files -i -c`), which is how a PWA icon directory gets accidentally orphaned.
/build/

# local safety-net backups (never commit)
.backups/

# Current probe/bench output (GPU detection, tier bench) — .txt report files in
# generated/ are committed occasionally and explicitly; this directory is written
# directly by the code running on the server.
generated/gpu/

# Portable CMS content snapshot written by scripts/export-content.js (the daily
# content backup) — a runtime artifact, never committed.
generated/content-export/

# Clarity Data-export API output (may contain analytics; never commit)
clarity-export/

# Alibaba Cloud AccessKey export — SECRET, never commit (see deploy/GCP-FREE-TIER.md)
AccessKey.csv
AccessKey-*.csv
*.AccessKey.csv
aliyun/credentials

# ─── Paths that already exist UNTRACKED on /opt/tukuk-os ────────────────────────────
# Measured 29 Oct 2026 (`git status --porcelain -uall` on the box): three netplan/NM yaml
# files under etc-netplan-reference/. They are the box's own network reference and nothing
# of theirs belongs in this repo — but the reason they are listed here is the deploy, not
# the tidiness: if a path with one of these names ever became tracked, `git merge --ff-only`
# on the box would refuse to create a file over the untracked one and the nightly update
# would stop, each run exiting 0. Ignoring them makes that unstageable by accident.
# Mind the asymmetry, also measured: an IGNORED path does not block the merge the way an
# untracked one does — a commit that adds it overwrites the server's copy and fast-forwards
# (scripts/ship-to-box.sh carries the numbers). So this rule protects the box by keeping the
# path out of the repo, not by keeping the repo out of the box.
# test/repo-ignore-hygiene.test.js pins this list against the box's measured state.
etc-netplan-reference/
